<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Disarm</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Assassin (guild level 4, up to 90%), Fighter (guild level 10), Thief (guild level 12, up to 70%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>disarm &lt;character&gt;
disarm                  (whoever you are fighting)
</pre>
<p>A quick move that strips the weapon from your foe's hands; it falls to the 
floor, and a monster will try to pick it up and wield it again. You must 
wield a weapon yourself, and your foe must wield one too. Your skill, 
dexterity and strength are matched against your foe's dexterity and 
strength.
</p><p>If you fail, nothing happens; but if you fail badly, your foe counters, and 
it is your own weapon that drops to the floor. A foe you have just 
disarmed, or who has just disarmed you, is on guard for a few combat 
rounds, and can't be disarmed again until then. Disarming takes endurance, 
and it starts a fight. You can disarm a sleeping foe without waking them. 
Other players only when both of you have signed the Book of Blood.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
